# The warm door at the bottom of the crypt (one-shot per save). Opened
# from code (MapComponent_TSC_WarmDoor) when a colonist first stands
# within 5 cells of the door; {PLAYER} is that pawn. Plays on both routes,
# and only after Old Wick's scene.
#
# The door is a REAL door on this same map, with the burial chamber behind
# it. Nothing here opens it: that is the player's move, and the shard and
# the sleeper are on the other side.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_WarmDoor

== start ==
The door is stone, and the stone is warm. Standing in front of it is like standing in front of a hearth with no fire.

{PLAYER} puts out a hand. The warmth comes through the glove. There is no handle and no hinge, but the stone gives under the pressure, a finger's width, the way a door does when it is not locked and never has been.

Something on the other side moves. Not footsteps. A weight, shifting, the way ice shifts on a lake.

* [Step back from the door.] -> end
* [It opens. Whatever is in there, it is not locked in.] -> end
